const PRIVACY = "This Privacy Policy explains how Roos Leeuwen (the “Operator”, “we”, “us” or “our”) handles information in connection with the mobile application (the “Application”). We aim to limit data processing to what is necessary for device connectivity, user-requested functions, subscriptions and support. This Policy also explains when Apple, Apphud, Google technologies, websites and television devices may process information independently.\n\n## Controller and contact information\n\nRoos Leeuwen, Frederiksplein 1C, 9724 NH Groningen, Netherlands, is responsible for personal data processed by the Operator in connection with the Application. Contact: roosapp@leeuwen.buzz. Third-party providers may act as separate controllers or service providers for their own operations, as described below.\n\n## Data minimization and Application architecture\n\nThe Application does not require registration or a developer-operated account. It has no Operator-managed backend, Firebase integration, separate analytics service, advertising, push-notification service, AI generation or AI chat, or dedicated third-party crash-reporting service. We do not use the Application to build advertising profiles or intentionally collect email addresses, advertising identifiers or other identifiers for marketing.\n\nThis does not mean that no technical information is processed anywhere: local device discovery and selected casting functions use network details, while Apple and Apphud may process purchase-related and technical information needed to operate subscriptions. Websites and receivers you choose to access may also collect information under their own policies.\n\n## Local network and connected devices\n\nWith the relevant iOS permission, the Application discovers compatible television and casting devices on your local Wi-Fi network. It may process local device details, names, network addresses and connection status to display available devices and send your requested remote-control or casting commands. The iOS Access Wi-Fi Information capability supports connection-related functionality in accordance with iOS restrictions.\n\nThese details are used for device discovery and operation on your phone and local network; they are not uploaded to an Operator-operated backend. If the local network permission is denied, device discovery and control may not function.\n\n## Photos, videos, files and screen mirroring\n\nWhen you choose to cast or share a photo, video or file, the Application accesses the selected content as needed to perform that action. The Application does not operate a cloud storage service for your content. User content and any locally saved Application information remain on the device, except for information transferred by your chosen connection to a television or accessed through a third-party service.\n\nScreen mirroring uses the system’s screen-sharing functionality. The displayed image is conveyed using the applicable system and receiving-device mechanisms, not through a backend operated by us. You control what you display, and people who can see the television may also see mirrored content.\n\n## Voice button and television assistant\n\nThe on-screen microphone button instructs the television to open its supported voice-assistant function, such as Google Assistant. The Application does not request access to, record from or otherwise process the iPhone microphone. Spoken commands are given through the television or its physical remote and may be processed by the television manufacturer or voice-assistant provider under their separate policies.\n\n## Built-in browser and video casting\n\nWebsites visited in the built-in browser load on your iPhone and may receive standard connection information such as your IP address and information sent by the browser. Sites may use cookies, local storage or similar technologies under their own privacy policies. The Operator does not run a server that receives your general browser history.\n\nTo make browser video casting available, a script checks the page for HTML video elements and direct HTTP or HTTPS media addresses. When you expressly select Cast, the chosen video address is sent via Google Cast technology to the selected compatible receiver (using the Google Default Media Receiver). The television then requests the media from the original hosting server, which may receive the television’s network and request information. The Application does not proxy the media stream through the iPhone.\n\nAccess to YouTube and other third-party sites is subject to those providers’ technologies, notices and policies. A page or stream without a usable direct media address, including many protected or blob-based streams, may not be cast using this feature.\n\n## Subscriptions and Apphud\n\nSubscriptions are purchased and billed through Apple’s in-app purchase system. We use Apphud SDK to help manage subscription entitlements and their status. In providing those functions, Apple and Apphud may process purchase identifiers, subscription status and limited device, app or network-related technical information required for the transaction and service operation. The precise information handled by those providers depends on their systems and applicable privacy policies.\n\nWe do not receive your full payment card details from Apple. We do not use Apphud as a separate general-purpose analytics platform for the Application, and we do not display advertisements. Apple and Apphud may maintain their own transaction or service records independently of locally stored Application data.\n\n## Information you send to support\n\nIf you email support, we receive the contact details and information you choose to include, such as your email address, message and any attachments. We use this information to respond, troubleshoot and keep necessary correspondence. Please avoid sending passwords, full payment card numbers or other sensitive information.\n\n## Purposes and legal bases\n\nWhere the EU General Data Protection Regulation applies, we process information as needed to deliver requested Application functions and subscription access (performance of a contract), to respond to support requests and maintain service security (our legitimate interests, balanced against your rights), and to comply with applicable legal obligations. Where a particular permission or consent is required, we rely on the applicable iOS choice or obtain consent as required by law. Third parties determine their own legal bases for independent processing.\n\n## Who may receive information\n\n**Your selected devices and content hosts.** Local device messages, selected content or chosen video addresses may reach the television or receiver; a media host may receive a direct request from that receiver.\n\n**Apple and Apphud.** They process purchase and subscription-related data under their applicable terms and privacy notices.\n\n**Google technology and external services.** Google Cast, device-based assistant services, YouTube and other sites may process data needed for their own operation when you use those features.\n\n**Service and legal recipients.** We may disclose support correspondence where necessary to operate email support, comply with a lawful request or protect legal rights, subject to applicable law.\n\nWe do not sell personal information or share it with advertising networks for targeted advertising.\n\n## Storage, retention and deletion\n\nApplication content and settings stored locally generally remain on your iPhone. Removing the Application normally removes its locally stored data, subject to iOS backup, restoration and other platform mechanisms. We do not provide a remote deletion button for data stored solely on your device, and we do not claim that removal deletes all information held independently by Apple, Apphud, television manufacturers or visited websites.\n\nSupport correspondence is retained only as reasonably necessary for support, legitimate recordkeeping and applicable legal obligations. Purchase records are subject to Apple’s and Apphud’s separate retention practices. You may manage supported local permissions and browser-related data through available Application and iOS controls.\n\n## International processing\n\nApple, Apphud, Google or external websites may process information in countries outside the European Economic Area, depending on their services and your use. Where we transfer personal information under our control internationally, we apply a lawful transfer mechanism and appropriate safeguards where required. Independent third-party transfers are governed by those providers’ policies.\n\n## Your privacy rights\n\nDepending on applicable law, you may request access to, correction or deletion of personal information we control; restriction of or objection to certain processing; and portability where relevant. Where processing relies on consent, you may withdraw it without affecting earlier lawful processing. You may contact us at roosapp@leeuwen.buzz to exercise your rights. We may need reasonable information to verify a request.\n\nBecause much of the Application’s information stays exclusively on your device, we may not have a server-side copy to retrieve or erase. Requests concerning data independently held by Apple, Apphud, Google, a website or a television provider may need to be directed to that provider. You also have the right to lodge a complaint with a competent data protection authority, including the Dutch Data Protection Authority (Autoriteit Persoonsgegevens).\n\n## Security and children\n\nWe seek to use reasonable security measures appropriate to an Application that operates primarily through iOS and local-network connections. No device, connection or third-party service is completely secure. The Application does not provide user accounts or features intended to solicit children’s personal information. Parents and guardians should supervise children’s access to external websites and video content.\n\n## Google TV brand authorization\n\nThe Google TV name and related licensed brand elements are used in the Application under a signed trademark licence and brand authorization agreement with Google LLC. This brand authorization concerns the permitted use of those trademarks; it does not make Google LLC the controller of personal information processed by the Operator. Google services and devices may handle information separately under their own privacy terms when you use them.\n\n## Updates to this Privacy Policy\n\nWe may revise this Policy to reflect changes to the Application, third-party services or legal requirements. The current version will be made available through an appropriate channel and identified by its “Last updated” date. If a change requires consent or another specific notice, we will comply with applicable law.\n\n## Contact\n\nRoos Leeuwen · Frederiksplein 1C, 9724 NH Groningen, Netherlands · roosapp@leeuwen.buzz";

const TERMS = "These Terms of Use (the “Terms”) govern access to and use of the mobile application (the “Application”) provided by Roos Leeuwen, an individual based in Groningen, the Netherlands (“we”, “us” or “our”). By using the Application, you agree to these Terms. If you do not agree, do not use the Application.\n\n## Operator and contact information\n\nThe Application is operated by Roos Leeuwen, Frederiksplein 1C, 9724 NH Groningen, Netherlands. For questions concerning the Application or these Terms, contact roosapp@leeuwen.buzz.\n\n## Purpose and principal features\n\nThe Application helps users interact with compatible Google TV, Android TV and Chromecast-enabled devices using an iPhone and a suitable Wi-Fi connection. Depending on the device and its capabilities, functions may include remote power and volume controls, mute, directional navigation, touchpad and keyboard input, device discovery and connection, photo and video casting, screen mirroring, and transferring selected files to a television.\n\nA microphone button in the on-screen remote may invoke Google Assistant on the television. The Application does not record speech through the iPhone microphone; voice interaction, where available, uses the television or its physical remote and is governed by the relevant device and service settings.\n\nAvailable features differ across television models, operating systems, local networks and regions. The Application is not a replacement for every function of an original television remote.\n\n## Connection requirements and system access\n\nYou are responsible for having compatible devices, a functioning local network and appropriate permissions. The Application uses local network access to discover and communicate with selected devices and has the iOS Access Wi-Fi Information capability for connection-related functionality. You can manage relevant permissions in iOS Settings; denying access may prevent device discovery or control.\n\nScreen mirroring uses a system-provided mechanism, subject to the availability and limitations of iOS and the receiving device. Availability of casting and remote-control functions also depends on third-party device software and network conditions.\n\n## Browser, video casting and third-party content\n\nThe Application includes a browser that opens websites on the iPhone. A displayed page may be shown on a television through screen mirroring. To offer video casting from the browser, the Application checks page video elements for a direct HTTP or HTTPS media address. Where such an address is found, a Cast control may be offered.\n\nWhen you choose Cast, the selected media address is passed through Google Cast technology to a compatible receiver. The television or receiver then requests the video directly from the original content server; the Application does not proxy the video stream through the iPhone. Videos that do not expose a directly usable address, including many blob-based or protected streams, may not support this feature.\n\nThe browser may provide access to external websites and services, including YouTube where available. Their content, account requirements, availability, tracking practices, copyright restrictions, streaming protections and terms are controlled by their respective providers. We do not guarantee that any third-party website, video, platform or streaming service will support playback, mirroring or casting.\n\n## Subscriptions, renewals and payments\n\nCertain features may require a paid subscription purchased through Apple’s in-app purchase system. At present, the Application offers subscriptions without a free trial and does not display advertising. The price, billing period and specific subscription entitlements are presented before purchase in the Application and the applicable Apple purchase interface.\n\nUnless otherwise stated in the purchase interface, subscriptions automatically renew for the same billing period until cancelled. Apple handles payment, renewal, account-level subscription management and applicable refunds under its terms. You can manage or cancel an active subscription in your Apple Account subscription settings. Deleting the Application does not cancel a subscription.\n\nWe use Apphud for subscription status, entitlement management and related purchase functionality. Subscription availability and prices may vary by country, currency and Apple storefront. Consumer rights provided by applicable law remain unaffected.\n\n## No account or registration\n\nThe Application does not require a developer-operated account or user registration. An Apple Account may be required to make and manage an in-app purchase. Third-party websites or television services may separately require their own accounts.\n\n## Your files, media and rights\n\nYou remain responsible for the photographs, videos, files, websites and other content that you choose to access, display or transmit. You confirm that you have the rights or permissions needed for your use of that content. The Application does not confer permission to copy, broadcast, download, redistribute or circumvent protections on content owned by third parties.\n\nMedia and settings handled by the Application are kept locally to the extent described in the Privacy Policy. Sending selected content or a media address to a television is initiated by you; the receiving device and any original content server may process that request independently.\n\n## Google TV trademark and brand authorization\n\nThe Google TV name and associated licensed brand elements are used in the Application pursuant to a signed trademark licence and brand authorization agreement with Google LLC. Such authorization governs our permitted use of the licensed branding in connection with the Application. Google LLC retains ownership of its trademarks and other intellectual property.\n\nThe Application is made available by Roos Leeuwen, who is responsible for these Terms and its operation. The trademark authorization does not make Google LLC a party to these Terms, transfer Google’s trademarks to users or grant users any independent right to use Google branding.\n\n## Acceptable use\n\nYou must use the Application lawfully and only with devices and networks you are entitled to access. You must not use it to interfere with other devices or networks, bypass access controls or digital rights management, infringe intellectual property rights, distribute harmful software, or violate a third-party platform’s terms.\n\n## Availability, updates and changes to features\n\nWe may maintain, improve, change, suspend or discontinue functions for security, technical, contractual or operational reasons, subject to applicable consumer law. Features dependent on Google Cast, Google Assistant, iOS, television firmware or external websites may change or stop working without our control. The Application is not currently offered through the App Store in Russia; availability elsewhere depends on local law and the Apple storefront.\n\n## Intellectual property\n\nExcept for your own content and third-party materials, the Application’s software, design and other protected elements belong to us or our licensors. You receive a limited, personal, non-exclusive, non-transferable licence to use the Application on devices that you own or control, consistent with these Terms and applicable Apple rules. You may not copy, modify, reverse-engineer or distribute the Application except where mandatory law expressly allows it.\n\n## Disclaimers and responsibility\n\nWe use reasonable care in providing the Application, but cannot promise uninterrupted operation, universal device compatibility or continuous availability of third-party services and content. To the fullest extent permitted by applicable law, we are not responsible for failures caused by third-party websites, device manufacturers, network operators or services outside our control.\n\nNothing in these Terms excludes or limits liability that cannot legally be excluded, including mandatory consumer rights or liability for intentional misconduct where applicable. Any limitation of liability is subject to the law that protects you as a consumer.\n\n## Suspension and termination\n\nYou may stop using and remove the Application at any time. We may restrict use when reasonably necessary to address unlawful conduct, serious misuse or security threats, subject to applicable law. Removal or restricted access does not itself cancel an Apple-managed subscription; cancellation must be made through Apple.\n\n## Governing law and consumer protections\n\nThese Terms are governed by the laws of the Netherlands, without depriving consumers of mandatory protections under the laws of their country of habitual residence where those protections apply. Disputes may be brought before courts having jurisdiction under applicable consumer protection rules.\n\n## Changes to these Terms\n\nWe may update these Terms to reflect changes in features, services, legal requirements or business practices. The revised version will be made available through an appropriate channel, with an updated “Last updated” date. Where law requires advance notice or your consent to a material change, we will follow those requirements.\n\n## Contact\n\nRoos Leeuwen · Frederiksplein 1C, 9724 NH Groningen, Netherlands · roosapp@leeuwen.buzz";

